# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title #
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error suppression and tailoring {#error-suppression-and-tailoring}"
msgstr "Penyekatan dan penyesuaian ralat {#error-suppression-and-tailoring}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Error suppression can refer to any technique that anticipates and tries to avoid certain types of noise and errors. This is easiest to explain through concrete examples, but keep in mind that these methods are not limited to the examples shown here, and new methods are continually being explored. Sometimes it is not possible to suppress errors, but it is possible to affect how they accumulate. If we can make errors accumulate more slowly, we might describe this as suppressing the overall error, but it is more accurately viewed as noise tailoring. In this lesson we cover canonical examples of error suppression (dynamical decoupling) and of noise tailoring/shaping (Pauli twirling).\n"
msgstr "Penyekatan ralat boleh merujuk kepada mana-mana teknik yang menjangka dan cuba mengelakkan jenis hingar dan ralat tertentu. Ini paling mudah diterangkan melalui contoh konkrit, tetapi ingat bahawa kaedah ini tidak terhad kepada contoh yang ditunjukkan di sini, dan kaedah baharu sentiasa diterokai. Kadangkala tidak mungkin untuk menyekat ralat, tetapi mungkin untuk mempengaruhi cara ia terkumpul. Jika kita boleh membuat ralat terkumpul dengan lebih perlahan, kita mungkin menggambarkan ini sebagai menyekat ralat keseluruhan, tetapi ia lebih tepat dilihat sebagai penyesuaian hingar. Dalam pelajaran ini kami merangkumi contoh kanonik penyekatan ralat (penyahgandingan dinamik) dan penyesuaian/pembentukan hingar (Pauli twirling).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "A video to accompany this lesson will launch in the next few days, and will be embedded here.\n"
msgstr "Video untuk melengkapi pelajaran ini akan dilancarkan dalam beberapa hari akan datang, dan akan dibenamkan di sini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling {#dynamical-decoupling}"
msgstr "Penyahgandingan dinamik {#dynamical-decoupling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us begin with a very simple state on a single qubit, and introduce a simple noise model. This is insufficient to completely explain dynamical decoupling, but it gives us a clear example. Suppose we have a qubit prepared in a superposition state using a Hadamard gate:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita mulakan dengan keadaan yang sangat mudah pada satu qubit, dan perkenalkan model hingar yang mudah. Ini tidak mencukupi untuk menerangkan sepenuhnya penyahgandingan dinamik, tetapi ia memberi kita contoh yang jelas. Andaikan kita mempunyai qubit yang disediakan dalam keadaan superposisi menggunakan get Hadamard:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( |0\\rangle +|1\\rangle \\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi\\rangle = H|0\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( |0\\rangle +|1\\rangle \\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This state is visualized on the Bloch sphere as shown below on the left. In the ideal case with zero noise, this qubit would remain in this state until the next operation is carried out. However, we know from the previous lesson that this is not what we observe. Noise causes the quantum information to degrade.\n"
msgstr "Keadaan ini divisualisasikan pada sfera Bloch seperti yang ditunjukkan di bawah di sebelah kiri. Dalam kes ideal dengan sifar hingar, qubit ini akan kekal dalam keadaan ini sehingga operasi seterusnya dijalankan. Walau bagaimanapun, kita tahu daripada pelajaran sebelumnya bahawa ini bukan apa yang kita perhatikan. Hingar menyebabkan maklumat kuantum merosot.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A Bloch sphere with a state vector initially equal to the plus state. The state then precesses around the z axis while remaining in the xy plane, consistent with time evolution in the presence of a magnetic field oriented along the z axis.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/precess.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A Bloch sphere with a state vector initially equal to the plus state. The state then precesses around the z axis while remaining in the xy plane, consistent with time evolution in the presence of a magnetic field oriented along the z axis.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/precess.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Noise or environmental coupling can cause the relative phase between the basis states to change. That is, the probabilities of $|0\\rangle$ and $|1\\rangle$ do not change, as the absolute values of their coefficients do not change. Rather, the phases of the amplitudes change, altering their real and imaginary components. To make this discussion more concrete, let us consider one type of interaction that can cause this: coupling to a magnetic field oriented in the Z direction: $\\vec{B} = (0,0,B_0)$.\n"
msgstr "Hingar atau gandingan persekitaran boleh menyebabkan fasa relatif antara keadaan asas berubah. Iaitu, kebarangkalian $|0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\rangle$ tidak berubah, kerana nilai mutlak pekali mereka tidak berubah. Sebaliknya, fasa amplitud berubah, mengubah komponen nyata dan khayalan mereka. Untuk menjadikan perbincangan ini lebih konkrit, mari kita pertimbangkan satu jenis interaksi yang boleh menyebabkan ini: gandingan kepada medan magnet yang berorientasikan dalam arah Z: $\\vec{B} = (0,0,B_0)$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider what happens to the state $|+\\rangle$ as time passes:\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan apa yang berlaku kepada keadaan $|+\\rangle$ apabila masa berlalu:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(t)\\rangle = e^{-iHt/\\hbar}|\\psi(0)\\rangle \\rightarrow e^{-iZ\\omega_B t/2}|\\psi(0)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(t)\\rangle = e^{-iHt/\\hbar}|\\psi(0)\\rangle \\rightarrow e^{-iZ\\omega_B t/2}|\\psi(0)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we have used the fact that a magnetic field in the Z direction causes precession about the Z axis with a frequency $\\omega_B$ that depends on the effective magnetic moment and magnetic field strength. The details are less important than the fact that this interaction causes evolution about the Z axis, resulting in opposite phase accumulation for the two computational basis states. Applying this operator to each term in $|\\psi\\rangle$, we find the following:\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita telah menggunakan fakta bahawa medan magnet dalam arah Z menyebabkan presesi mengelilingi paksi Z dengan frekuensi $\\omega_B$ yang bergantung pada momen magnet berkesan dan kekuatan medan magnet. Butiran adalah kurang penting berbanding fakta bahawa interaksi ini menyebabkan evolusi mengelilingi paksi Z, menghasilkan pengumpulan fasa bertentangan untuk kedua-dua keadaan asas pengkomputeran. Menggunakan operator ini kepada setiap sebutan dalam $|\\psi\\rangle$, kita dapati yang berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(t)\\rangle = e^{-iZ\\omega_B t/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( |0\\rangle +|1\\rangle \\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t/2}|0\\rangle +e^{i\\omega_B t/2}|1\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(t)\\rangle = e^{-iZ\\omega_B t/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( |0\\rangle +|1\\rangle \\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t/2}|0\\rangle +e^{i\\omega_B t/2}|1\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This time-dependent phase corresponds to precession about the Z axis in the Bloch sphere picture. This is shown in the right half of the figure above.\n"
msgstr "Fasa bergantung masa ini sepadan dengan presesi mengelilingi paksi Z dalam gambaran sfera Bloch. Ini ditunjukkan pada separuh kanan rajah di atas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we knew that this interaction were occurring in a controlled way, we could predict it. To model this type of noise, we instead consider a distribution of possible magnetic field strengths, each occurring with some classical probability (other sources of noise would need to be modeled differently). We need to consider what happens when there is a non-zero classical probability that the state has not rotated at all, and also some probability that it has rotated by a small amount, or even by a large amount. This distribution of possible rotations is the reason for the spreading of the state in the Bloch sphere picture below. If there is more such dephasing noise, the phase will be less well-defined. In the limit of strong dephasing, the qubit becomes completely dephased, corresponding to the loss of the quantum coherence stored in the state.\n"
msgstr "Jika kita tahu bahawa interaksi ini berlaku dengan cara yang terkawal, kita boleh meramalkannya. Untuk memodelkan jenis hingar ini, kita sebaliknya mempertimbangkan taburan kekuatan medan magnet yang mungkin, setiap satu berlaku dengan kebarangkalian klasik tertentu (sumber hingar lain perlu dimodelkan secara berbeza). Kita perlu mempertimbangkan apa yang berlaku apabila terdapat kebarangkalian klasik bukan sifar bahawa keadaan tidak berputar langsung, dan juga sesetengah kebarangkalian bahawa ia telah berputar sedikit, atau bahkan dengan banyak. Taburan putaran yang mungkin ini adalah sebab penyebaran keadaan dalam gambaran sfera Bloch di bawah. Jika terdapat lebih banyak hingar penyahfasaan sebegini, fasa akan menjadi kurang jelas takrifannya. Dalam had penyahfasaan kuat, qubit menjadi sepenuhnya dinyahfasakan, sepadan dengan kehilangan koherens kuantum yang disimpan dalam keadaan tersebut.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Three panels, each showing a Bloch sphere. The first shows a pure quantum state vector, the plus state. The second shows a broadened, shorter region of state space, indicating a mixed state with imperfect phase information. The third shows a tiny region near the origin corresponding to complete dephasing.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/dephasing.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Three panels, each showing a Bloch sphere. The first shows a pure quantum state vector, the plus state. The second shows a broadened, shorter region of state space, indicating a mixed state with imperfect phase information. The third shows a tiny region near the origin corresponding to complete dephasing.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/dephasing.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Of course, in an experiment we have no idea what random coupling will occur. What can we do about this?\n"
msgstr "Sudah tentu, dalam eksperimen kita tidak tahu gandingan rawak apa yang akan berlaku. Apa yang boleh kita lakukan mengenai ini?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Suppose that the environmental coupling remains approximately constant over a time interval $2t_0$. Consider what would happen if we followed this prescription:\n"
msgstr "Andaikan gandingan persekitaran kekal kira-kira malar sepanjang selang masa $2t_0$. Pertimbangkan apa yang akan berlaku jika kita mengikut preskripsi ini:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Allow the phase to change for time $t_0$\n"
msgstr "Benarkan fasa berubah untuk masa $t_0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply an X gate to the qubit\n"
msgstr "Gunakan get X pada qubit\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Allow the same environmental coupling to occur for a further time $t_0$\n"
msgstr "Benarkan gandingan persekitaran yang sama berlaku untuk masa lanjutan $t_0$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "Apply a second X gate\n"
msgstr "Gunakan get X kedua\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After the initial time evolution, we would have exactly the state above. Applying the first X gate we have:\n"
msgstr "Selepas evolusi masa awal, kita akan mempunyai tepat keadaan di atas. Menggunakan get X pertama kita ada:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X|\\psi(t_0)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X|\\psi(t_0)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now when the second interval of $t_0$ passes, the same interaction takes place. But now the amplitudes are associated with the opposite Z eigenstates, meaning the sign of the rotation about the Z axis has switched. After allowing the system to evolve in time for another $t_0$ we have the state:\n"
msgstr "Kini apabila selang kedua $t_0$ berlalu, interaksi yang sama berlaku. Tetapi kini amplitud dikaitkan dengan eigenstate Z yang bertentangan, bermakna tanda putaran mengelilingi paksi Z telah bertukar. Selepas membenarkan sistem berkembang dalam masa untuk $t_0$ yang lain kita ada keadaan:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-iZ\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +e^{i\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
"And inserting $t = 2t_0$ we have:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(2t_0)\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|1\\rangle +|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-iZ\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +e^{i\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
"Dan memasukkan $t = 2t_0$ kita ada:\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(2t_0)\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|1\\rangle +|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the final X gate does nothing in this case, but it is generally necessary:\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan get X terakhir tidak melakukan apa-apa dalam kes ini, tetapi ia amnya diperlukan:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(2t_0)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\rangle +|1\\rangle \\right) = |\\psi(t=0)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(2t_0)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\rangle +|1\\rangle \\right) = |\\psi(t=0)\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We have recovered the original quantum state, including its relative phase. This process is an especially simple example of dynamical decoupling.\n"
msgstr "Kita telah memulihkan keadaan kuantum asal, termasuk fasa relatifnya. Proses ini adalah contoh yang amat mudah bagi penyahgandingan dinamik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "More generally, __dynamical decoupling__ (DD) involves inserting some single-qubit gates to reduce the effect of interactions with systems outside the qubit (decoupling it from the environment). The complete refocusing of all possible phase histories back to the original state, as shown above, is somewhat idealized, but it is still a possible scenario. Let's discuss when DD is useful and what caveats exist.\n"
msgstr "Secara lebih umum, __penyahgandingan dinamik__ (DD) melibatkan penyisipan beberapa get satu-qubit untuk mengurangkan kesan interaksi dengan sistem di luar qubit (menyahgandingkannya daripada persekitaran). Penumpuan semula sepenuhnya bagi semua sejarah fasa yang mungkin kembali kepada keadaan asal, seperti yang ditunjukkan di atas, agak diidealkan, tetapi ia masih senario yang mungkin. Mari kita bincangkan bila DD berguna dan apakah amaran yang wujud.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In the text above, we stepped through the effect of an `XX` DD sequence on the initial state $|+\\rangle$. Check whether the same steps above also return the state $|+i\\rangle$ back to its initial state under the same assumptions of a slowly-varying magnetic field along the z direction.\n"
msgstr "Dalam teks di atas, kami melangkah melalui kesan jujukan DD `XX` pada keadaan awal $|+\\rangle$. Semak sama ada langkah yang sama di atas juga mengembalikan keadaan $|+i\\rangle$ kembali kepada keadaan awalnya di bawah andaian yang sama iaitu medan magnet yang berubah perlahan sepanjang arah z.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Answer\">\n"
msgstr ""
"<Accordion>\n"
"<AccordionItem title=\"Jawapan\">\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(t)\\rangle = e^{-iZ\\omega_B t/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( |0\\rangle +i|1\\rangle \\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t/2}|0\\rangle +i e^{i\\omega_B t/2}|1\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(t)\\rangle = e^{-iZ\\omega_B t/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( |0\\rangle +i|1\\rangle \\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t/2}|0\\rangle +i e^{i\\omega_B t/2}|1\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"X|\\psi(t_0)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +i e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"X|\\psi(t_0)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +i e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-iZ\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +i e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +i e^{i\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
"And inserting $t = 2t_0$ we have\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(2t_0)\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|1\\rangle +i |0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"e^{-iZ\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +i e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left( e^{-i\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}e^{i\\omega_B t_0/2}|1\\rangle +i e^{i\\omega_B (t-t_0)/2}e^{-i\\omega_B t_0/2}|0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"
"Dan memasukkan $t = 2t_0$ kita ada\n"
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(2t_0)\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|1\\rangle +i |0\\rangle \\right)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Applying the final X gate, we have:\n"
msgstr "Menggunakan get X terakhir, kita ada:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(2t_0)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\rangle +i |1\\rangle \\right) = |\\psi(t=0)\\rangle = |+i\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi(2t_0)\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\rangle +i |1\\rangle \\right) = |\\psi(t=0)\\rangle = |+i\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"</AccordionItem>\n"
"</Accordion>\n"
msgstr ""

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "When to use DD {#when-to-use-dd}"
msgstr "Bila menggunakan DD {#when-to-use-dd}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The first and most obvious caveat is that we assumed a purely dephasing channel in our treatment. Real-world interactions typically produce a mixture of dephasing and other error mechanisms. In the treatment above, we chose to apply X gates specifically. This is referred to as an `XX` sequence in dynamical decoupling. This particular sequence is appropriate for purely dephasing errors. But there are other sequences that might be more broadly applicable, like `XY4` (shown in the circuit diagram below) and the more complex `XY8`.\n"
msgstr "Amaran pertama dan paling jelas ialah kita mengandaikan saluran penyahfasaan tulen dalam rawatan kita. Interaksi dunia sebenar biasanya menghasilkan gabungan penyahfasaan dan mekanisme ralat lain. Dalam rawatan di atas, kami memilih untuk menggunakan get X secara khusus. Ini dirujuk sebagai jujukan `XX` dalam penyahgandingan dinamik. Jujukan tertentu ini sesuai untuk ralat penyahfasaan tulen. Tetapi terdapat jujukan lain yang mungkin lebih boleh digunakan secara meluas, seperti `XY4` (ditunjukkan dalam gambar rajah litar di bawah) dan `XY8` yang lebih kompleks.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit showing a sequence of four quantum gates used in dynamical decoupling: an X gate, a Y gate, a second X gate, and a second Y gate.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/xy4.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit showing a sequence of four quantum gates used in dynamical decoupling: an X gate, a Y gate, a second X gate, and a second Y gate.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/xy4.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Another caveat is that dynamical decoupling adds single-qubit gates, which can add single-qubit errors due to gate imperfections or even crosstalk. These single-qubit error rates are typically much lower than multi-qubit gate errors, so this is usually not a major concern, but it is something to keep in mind if many qubits are employing DD many times throughout your circuit.\n"
msgstr "Amaran lain ialah penyahgandingan dinamik menambah get satu-qubit, yang boleh menambah ralat satu-qubit disebabkan oleh ketidaksempurnaan get atau juga crosstalk. Kadar ralat satu-qubit ini biasanya jauh lebih rendah daripada ralat get berbilang-qubit, jadi ini biasanya bukan kebimbangan utama, tetapi ia adalah sesuatu yang perlu diingat jika banyak qubit menggunakan DD berkali-kali sepanjang litar anda.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "DD is useful when the external coupling has time to affect the state of the qubit. Because qubits are painstakingly well isolated and external couplings should be weak, this type of noise is most noticeable when a qubit sits idle for long periods. For short idle times, the effect of DD could be to add single-qubit gate errors while suppressing very little noise; the fidelity of your circuit could actually be reduced.\n"
msgstr "DD berguna apabila gandingan luaran mempunyai masa untuk mempengaruhi keadaan qubit. Kerana qubit disekat dengan teliti dan gandingan luaran sepatutnya lemah, jenis hingar ini paling ketara apabila qubit terbiar untuk tempoh yang lama. Untuk masa terbiar yang singkat, kesan DD boleh menambah ralat get satu-qubit sambil menyekat hingar yang sangat sedikit; ketepatan litar anda sebenarnya boleh berkurangan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "__Key takeaway__: Use dynamical decoupling when qubits remain idle for sufficiently long periods, and pay attention to the type of DD sequence being used.\n"
msgstr "__Perkara penting__: Gunakan penyahgandingan dinamik apabila qubit kekal terbiar untuk tempoh yang cukup lama, dan beri perhatian kepada jenis jujukan DD yang digunakan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Dynamical decoupling using Qiskit {#dynamical-decoupling-using-qiskit}"
msgstr "Penyahgandingan dinamik menggunakan Qiskit {#dynamical-decoupling-using-qiskit}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let us explore the use of DD by examining the case of several qubits prepared in the $|+\\rangle$ state, which then remain idle for a long time. In the absence of errors, preparing the multi-qubit state $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$ and then applying a Hadamard gate before measurement (thereby measuring in the X basis) should always yield 0. With noise, the measurement outcome will be 0 only a fraction of the time rather than with 100% probability. We calculate the average `X` expectation value across multiple qubits. That is, we are interested in the following:\n"
msgstr "Mari kita terokai penggunaan DD dengan mengkaji kes beberapa qubit yang disediakan dalam keadaan $|+\\rangle$, yang kemudian kekal terbiar untuk masa yang lama. Tanpa ralat, menyediakan keadaan berbilang-qubit $|\\psi\\rangle = |+\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$ dan kemudian menggunakan get Hadamard sebelum pengukuran (dengan itu mengukur dalam asas X) sepatutnya sentiasa menghasilkan 0. Dengan hingar, hasil pengukuran akan menjadi 0 hanya sebahagian daripada masa dan bukannya dengan kebarangkalian 100%. Kami mengira nilai jangkaan purata `X` merentas berbilang qubit. Iaitu, kami berminat dengan yang berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"f\\equiv \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}{\\langle\\Psi | X_j |\\Psi\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"f\\equiv \\frac{1}{N}\\sum_{j=0}^{N-1}{\\langle\\Psi | X_j |\\Psi\\rangle}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $X_j \\equiv III..X...II$ with the `X` operator in the $j^{th}$ position from the right and $|\\Psi\\rangle$ is the state of the entire system.\n"
msgstr "di mana $X_j \\equiv III..X...II$ dengan operator `X` pada kedudukan ke-$j^{th}$ dari kanan dan $|\\Psi\\rangle$ ialah keadaan keseluruhan sistem.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This circuit contains intentional delays, which is somewhat contrived for a benchmark. However, it is very common for real circuits to contain qubits that sit idle during part of the execution. You can think of this as a simplified model of a more complex circuit in which some qubits remain idle for part of the computation. This type of benchmarking based on the evolution of $|+\\rangle$ states is often referred to as _Ramsey benchmarking_.\n"
msgstr "Litar ini mengandungi kelewatan yang disengajakan, yang agak dibuat-buat untuk penanda aras. Walau bagaimanapun, adalah sangat biasa untuk litar sebenar mengandungi qubit yang terbiar semasa sebahagian daripada pelaksanaan. Anda boleh menganggap ini sebagai model ringkas bagi litar yang lebih kompleks di mana sesetengah qubit kekal terbiar untuk sebahagian daripada pengiraan. Jenis penanda aras ini berdasarkan evolusi keadaan $|+\\rangle$ sering dirujuk sebagai _penanda aras Ramsey_.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We begin by loading the necessary packages and configuring the service.\n"
msgstr "Kami bermula dengan memuatkan pakej yang diperlukan dan mengkonfigurasi perkhidmatan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we define some helper functions. First, we want to address the point about long idle times. What exactly does \"long\" mean in this context? We could simply report the idle time in microseconds. However, it is useful to know how many two-qubit gates could be executed during that same interval. This makes the idle times more directly indicative of the circuit depth that could have been executed during the same period. The first helper function gets the two-qubit gate native to the backend and determines the duration of that gate.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami mentakrifkan beberapa fungsi pembantu. Pertama, kami mahu menangani perkara mengenai masa terbiar yang lama. Apa sebenarnya maksud \"lama\" dalam konteks ini? Kami boleh sekadar melaporkan masa terbiar dalam mikrosaat. Walau bagaimanapun, berguna untuk mengetahui berapa banyak get dua-qubit yang boleh dilaksanakan sepanjang selang yang sama itu. Ini menjadikan masa terbiar lebih menunjukkan secara langsung kedalaman litar yang boleh dilaksanakan sepanjang tempoh yang sama. Fungsi pembantu pertama mendapatkan get dua-qubit asli kepada backend dan menentukan tempoh get tersebut.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The second function simply creates a Ramsey circuit (one with qubits in the $|+\\rangle$ state), implements a delay, rotates using an H gate, and then measures. Recall that a Hadamard gate (H) maps $|+\\rangle$ to $|0\\rangle$, so measuring $|0\\rangle$ in the `Z` basis after the Hadamard corresponds to the qubit having been in $|+\\rangle$ immediately before the Hadamard.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi kedua hanya mencipta litar Ramsey (satu dengan qubit dalam keadaan $|+\\rangle$), melaksanakan kelewatan, memutar menggunakan get H, dan kemudian mengukur. Ingat bahawa get Hadamard (H) memetakan $|+\\rangle$ kepada $|0\\rangle$, jadi mengukur $|0\\rangle$ dalam asas `Z` selepas Hadamard sepadan dengan qubit yang berada dalam $|+\\rangle$ sejurus sebelum Hadamard.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our final function converts the raw counts of 0 and 1 measurement outcomes into an expectation value of `X`.\n"
msgstr "Fungsi terakhir kami menukar kiraan mentah bagi hasil pengukuran 0 dan 1 kepada nilai jangkaan `X`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we specify the details of our test, including the number of qubits and the gate sequence to be used in DD (in this case `XX`). Note especially that we set the optimization level to zero. In practice, you would often select a higher optimization level; here we use level 0 to ensure that the effects of the errors targeted by DD remain visible. Finally, we determine the characteristic time for two-qubit gates on this backend and print some relevant times.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami menentukan butiran ujian kami, termasuk bilangan qubit dan jujukan get yang akan digunakan dalam DD (dalam kes ini `XX`). Perhatikan terutamanya bahawa kami menetapkan tahap pengoptimuman kepada sifar. Dalam praktiknya, anda sering akan memilih tahap pengoptimuman yang lebih tinggi; di sini kami menggunakan tahap 0 untuk memastikan kesan ralat yang disasarkan oleh DD kekal kelihatan. Akhir sekali, kami menentukan masa ciri untuk get dua-qubit pada backend ini dan mencetak beberapa masa yang berkaitan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now construct our circuits and transpile them for our chosen backend.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami membina litar kami dan mentranspil untuk backend pilihan kami.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We should visualize at least one circuit to ensure we have coded our circuit with the desired states and delays. It might be easier to visualize the pre-transpiled circuit `qc`, or you might check the transpiled one `qc_isa`.\n"
msgstr "Kami perlu memvisualisasikan sekurang-kurangnya satu litar untuk memastikan kami telah mengekod litar kami dengan keadaan dan kelewatan yang dikehendaki. Mungkin lebih mudah untuk memvisualisasikan litar pra-transpil `qc`, atau anda boleh menyemak litar yang ditranspil `qc_isa`.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/48a7cd69-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/48a7cd69-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Execute {#execute}"
msgstr "Laksanakan {#execute}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We're finally ready to execute on hardware. We use Sampler to obtain many measurements of each qubit, and we will use it twice: once with DD explicitly turned off, and once with DD turned on and using the `XX` gate sequence.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya kami bersedia untuk melaksanakan pada perkakasan. Kami menggunakan Sampler untuk mendapatkan banyak pengukuran bagi setiap qubit, dan kami akan menggunakannya dua kali: sekali dengan DD dimatikan secara eksplisit, dan sekali dengan DD dihidupkan dan menggunakan jujukan get `XX`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can extract the counts from the various circuits.\n"
msgstr "Kami boleh mengekstrak kiraan daripada pelbagai litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Post-processing {#post-processing}"
msgstr "Pasca-pemprosesan {#post-processing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now have the counts from the measurement, but we want to turn that into the expectation value of `X` and then average those expectation values across all the qubits we used, to learn about the preservation of phase information. For that we use our `counts_to_x_expectations` function defined earlier.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami mempunyai kiraan daripada pengukuran, tetapi kami mahu menukarkannya kepada nilai jangkaan `X` dan kemudian purata nilai jangkaan tersebut merentas semua qubit yang kami gunakan, untuk mengetahui tentang pemeliharaan maklumat fasa. Untuk itu kami menggunakan fungsi `counts_to_x_expectations` kami yang ditakrifkan sebelum ini.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, let's plot our results.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, mari kita plotkan hasil kami.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/f406833c-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/f406833c-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As you can see, with no explicit delay the expectation values are indeed near 1, which we would expect if all phase information were preserved. If all phase information were lost, there would be no preference for the final rotation to produce $|0\\rangle$ rather than $|1\\rangle$, and the average expectation value would approach zero. In the data, we see that as delay times increase, the average expectation value of `X` decreases, starting to approach zero. Note that DD has been very effective here; the expectation values with DD are typically more than 20% better (closer to 1) than the values without DD. But also note that the first delayed data point corresponds to a delay roughly equivalent to 100 two-qubit gate operations. This reinforces the point that DD is most useful when qubits remain idle for relatively long periods.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang anda lihat, tanpa kelewatan eksplisit, nilai jangkaan memang hampir dengan 1, yang kami jangkakan jika semua maklumat fasa dipelihara. Jika semua maklumat fasa hilang, tidak akan ada keutamaan untuk putaran akhir menghasilkan $|0\\rangle$ berbanding $|1\\rangle$, dan nilai jangkaan purata akan menghampiri sifar. Dalam data, kita lihat bahawa apabila masa kelewatan meningkat, nilai jangkaan purata `X` berkurangan, mula menghampiri sifar. Perhatikan bahawa DD sangat berkesan di sini; nilai jangkaan dengan DD biasanya lebih daripada 20% lebih baik (lebih hampir dengan 1) berbanding nilai tanpa DD. Tetapi perhatikan juga bahawa titik data pertama yang dilewatkan sepadan dengan kelewatan yang lebih kurang setara dengan 100 operasi get dua-qubit. Ini mengukuhkan lagi bahawa DD paling berguna apabila qubit kekal terbiar untuk tempoh yang agak lama.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-1}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-1}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we apply DD using `XY4` to the same circuit as before, do you expect it to yield results that are much better, much worse, or about the same, as DD using `XX`? Explain.\n"
msgstr "Jika kita menggunakan DD menggunakan `XY4` pada litar yang sama seperti sebelum ini, adakah anda menjangkakan ia akan menghasilkan keputusan yang jauh lebih baik, jauh lebih teruk, atau lebih kurang sama, seperti DD menggunakan `XX`? Terangkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "About the same, perhaps slightly worse. The circuit we used had states rotated into the XY plane. This state stores information primarily in its phase, making it especially sensitive to dephasing errors rather than T1 relaxation. XY4 might help with a wider variety of errors, but XX is already optimized to help the circuit we are using. XY4 might be just as good, but would not add anything substantial, or the fact that XY4 contains more gates might allow additional gate errors to make the results slightly worse.\n"
msgstr "Lebih kurang sama, mungkin sedikit lebih teruk. Litar yang kami gunakan mempunyai keadaan yang diputarkan ke dalam satah XY. Keadaan ini menyimpan maklumat terutamanya dalam fasanya, menjadikannya amat sensitif kepada ralat penyahfasaan berbanding pelonggaran T1. XY4 mungkin membantu dengan pelbagai jenis ralat yang lebih luas, tetapi XX sudah dioptimumkan untuk membantu litar yang kami gunakan. XY4 mungkin sama baiknya, tetapi tidak akan menambah apa-apa yang substansial, atau hakikat bahawa XY4 mengandungi lebih banyak get mungkin membolehkan ralat get tambahan menjadikan hasil sedikit lebih teruk.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The last result used the simplest DD gate sequence `XX`. Let's see how to implement a more complex sequence, `XY4`. We define a Sampler in the next section.\n"
msgstr "Hasil terakhir menggunakan jujukan get DD paling mudah `XX`. Mari kita lihat cara melaksanakan jujukan yang lebih kompleks, `XY4`. Kami mentakrifkan Sampler dalam bahagian seterusnya.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/c830c2ce-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/c830c2ce-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Here we see that `XY4` is not appreciably different from `XX`. It might be very slightly worse due to additional gates in the `XY4` sequence, but more importantly, we already explained why `XX` would have the desired effect in preserving phase specifically for a state like $|+\\rangle$. There is no reason to think that for such an initial state, a different sequence would improve results.\n"
msgstr "Di sini kita lihat bahawa `XY4` tidak jauh berbeza daripada `XX`. Ia mungkin sedikit lebih teruk disebabkan get tambahan dalam jujukan `XY4`, tetapi yang lebih penting, kami sudah menerangkan sebab `XX` akan mempunyai kesan yang dikehendaki dalam memelihara fasa khusus untuk keadaan seperti $|+\\rangle$. Tiada sebab untuk berfikir bahawa untuk keadaan awal sebegitu, jujukan yang berbeza akan meningkatkan hasil.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-2}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-2}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify that the `XY4` sequence leaves the state unchanged up to a global phase.\n"
msgstr "Sahkan bahawa jujukan `XY4` meninggalkan keadaan tidak berubah sehingga fasa global.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"YXYX|+\\rangle & = YXYX(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = YXY(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = YX(i|1\\rangle-i|0\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = Y(i|0\\rangle-i|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = (-|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& =-|+\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"YXYX|+\\rangle & = YXYX(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = YXY(|0\\rangle+|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = YX(i|1\\rangle-i|0\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = Y(i|0\\rangle-i|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& = (-|0\\rangle-|1\\rangle)\\\\\n"
"& =-|+\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"
msgstr "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We should begin by noting that Pauli twirling is often used not as an error-suppression technique, but as an error-shaping technique: it makes noise/errors behave differently, sometimes more predictably, to enable other methods. Although Pauli twirling does not *prevent* errors, it might prevent their coherent accumulation.\n"
msgstr "Kita perlu mulakan dengan menyatakan bahawa Pauli twirling sering digunakan bukan sebagai teknik penyekatan ralat, tetapi sebagai teknik pembentukan ralat: ia membuat hingar/ralat berkelakuan berbeza, kadangkala lebih boleh diramal, untuk membolehkan kaedah lain. Walaupun Pauli twirling tidak *menghalang* ralat, ia mungkin menghalang pengumpulan koheren mereka.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In a quantum circuit, multiple different sources of error add together. The errors can add in different ways, notably _coherently_ and _incoherently_. Coherent accumulation of errors means that noise or imperfect implementations all tend to drive errors in the same direction across multiple layers and gates. An example would be coherent over-rotation when applying a rotation gate.\n"
msgstr "Dalam litar kuantum, pelbagai sumber ralat yang berbeza bertambah bersama. Ralat boleh bertambah dengan cara yang berbeza, terutamanya _secara koheren_ dan _secara tidak koheren_. Pengumpulan koheren ralat bermaksud bahawa hingar atau pelaksanaan yang tidak sempurna semuanya cenderung untuk menggerakkan ralat dalam arah yang sama merentas berbilang lapisan dan get. Satu contoh ialah lebih-putaran koheren apabila menggunakan get putaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Consider an ideal rotation gate, such as $R_x(\\theta_0)$, which rotates about the X axis by exactly $\\theta_0$. Of course, gate implementation is not perfect, and the actual rotation might be $\\theta_0+\\Delta\\theta$ for one implementation, and it could even be the case that $\\Delta\\theta$ is always the same sign, and possibly similar in magnitude across many applications of $R_x(\\theta)$. Thus repeated application of rotation gates can result in coherent accumulation of these many over-rotations (or under-rotations), $\\Delta \\theta$.\n"
msgstr "Pertimbangkan get putaran ideal, seperti $R_x(\\theta_0)$, yang memutar mengelilingi paksi X dengan tepat $\\theta_0$. Sudah tentu, pelaksanaan get tidak sempurna, dan putaran sebenar mungkin $\\theta_0+\\Delta\\theta$ untuk satu pelaksanaan, dan mungkin juga berlaku bahawa $\\Delta\\theta$ sentiasa mempunyai tanda yang sama, dan mungkin serupa dari segi magnitud merentas banyak penggunaan $R_x(\\theta)$. Oleh itu penggunaan berulang get putaran boleh menghasilkan pengumpulan koheren bagi banyak lebih-putaran (atau kurang-putaran) ini, $\\Delta \\theta$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Incoherent error accumulation is just the opposite: errors in random directions with random signs, such that errors in different layers do not always interfere additively, but sometimes cancel or add in quadrature. Clearly incoherent errors accumulate more slowly in terms of the overall effect on the state of the qubit. A toy diagram of this is shown in the figure below. This is a simplification. Real quantum errors are not restricted to a two-dimensional Cartesian space; not all error contributions will have the same magnitude, and there are more complexities. But the intuition of a picture like this is useful: coherent errors tend to accumulate faster than incoherent ones.\n"
msgstr "Pengumpulan ralat tidak koheren adalah sebaliknya: ralat dalam arah rawak dengan tanda rawak, sedemikian rupa sehingga ralat dalam lapisan berbeza tidak sentiasa mengganggu secara aditif, tetapi kadangkala saling batal atau bertambah secara kuadratur. Jelas sekali ralat tidak koheren terkumpul dengan lebih perlahan dari segi kesan keseluruhan pada keadaan qubit. Rajah mainan ini ditunjukkan dalam rajah di bawah. Ini adalah penyederhanaan. Ralat kuantum sebenar tidak terhad kepada ruang Cartesian dua dimensi; tidak semua sumbangan ralat akan mempunyai magnitud yang sama, dan terdapat lebih banyak kerumitan. Tetapi intuisi gambaran sebegini adalah berguna: ralat koheren cenderung terkumpul lebih cepat daripada ralat tidak koheren.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Two images. First, vectors denoting errors arranged in a line such that they add up coherently to a large error. Second, vectors in random directions being added to yield a smaller net effect, as in incoherent error accumulation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/accumulation.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Two images. First, vectors denoting errors arranged in a line such that they add up coherently to a large error. Second, vectors in random directions being added to yield a smaller net effect, as in incoherent error accumulation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/accumulation.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One can often obtain higher-fidelity results by turning coherent error accumulation into incoherent error accumulation. A primary way of accomplishing this is called __Pauli twirling__.\n"
msgstr "Seseorang selalunya boleh mendapatkan hasil dengan ketepatan lebih tinggi dengan menukar pengumpulan ralat koheren kepada pengumpulan ralat tidak koheren. Cara utama untuk mencapai ini dipanggil __Pauli twirling__.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling refers to adding combinations of Pauli gates $P \\in \\{X, Y, Z, I\\}$ before and after a desired gate operation $U$ in such a way that $P_1 U P_2 = U$. Here, $P_1$ and $P_2$ are not single Paulis, but collections of Pauli operators often acting on multiple qubits. You might sometimes see it stated that the action of the extra Pauli gates is \"equivalent to the identity\". But this is imprecise and potentially confusing. The Pauli gates are separated by $U$ and the goal is to leave the logical action of all gates equal to $U$. Sometimes $U$ is called the \"payload\" to distinguish this intended operation from the gates added for suppression. Some examples of Pauli twirling around a CNOT gate are shown below.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling merujuk kepada penambahan gabungan get Pauli $P \\in \\{X, Y, Z, I\\}$ sebelum dan selepas operasi get yang dikehendaki $U$ sedemikian rupa sehingga $P_1 U P_2 = U$. Di sini, $P_1$ dan $P_2$ bukan Pauli tunggal, tetapi koleksi operator Pauli yang selalunya bertindak pada berbilang qubit. Anda kadangkala mungkin melihat ia dinyatakan bahawa tindakan get Pauli tambahan adalah \"setara dengan identiti\". Tetapi ini tidak tepat dan berpotensi mengelirukan. Get Pauli dipisahkan oleh $U$ dan matlamatnya adalah untuk meninggalkan tindakan logik semua get sama dengan $U$. Kadangkala $U$ dipanggil \"muatan\" untuk membezakan operasi yang dimaksudkan ini daripada get yang ditambah untuk penyekatan. Beberapa contoh Pauli twirling mengelilingi get CNOT ditunjukkan di bawah.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Four images showing pieces of four quantum circuits, each with two qubits. The first is a simple CNOT gate. The others each show a CNOT gate but surrounded by Pauli gates in a way that preserves the overall logic of a CNOT operation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/twirl-4.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Four images showing pieces of four quantum circuits, each with two qubits. The first is a simple CNOT gate. The others each show a CNOT gate but surrounded by Pauli gates in a way that preserves the overall logic of a CNOT operation.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/twirl-4.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's walk through just one example to verify that twirling leaves the logical effect of the payload unchanged.\n"
"Without loss of generality, let the two-qubit states involving $q_0$ and $q_1$ be:\n"
msgstr ""
"Mari kita lalui hanya satu contoh untuk mengesahkan bahawa twirling meninggalkan kesan logik muatan tidak berubah.\n"
"Tanpa kehilangan keumuman, biarkan keadaan dua-qubit yang melibatkan $q_0$ dan $q_1$ ialah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_\\text{init}\\rangle = a|00\\rangle + b|01\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_\\text{init}\\rangle = a|00\\rangle + b|01\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|11\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As always, we are using the qubit ordering convention $|q_1,q_0\\rangle$. Applying a CX gate with $q_1$ as the target yields\n"
msgstr "Seperti biasa, kami menggunakan konvensyen susunan qubit $|q_1,q_0\\rangle$. Menggunakan get CX dengan $q_1$ sebagai sasaran menghasilkan\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"CX|\\psi_\\text{init}\\rangle = |\\psi_\\text{final}\\rangle = a|00\\rangle + b|11\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|01\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"CX|\\psi_\\text{init}\\rangle = |\\psi_\\text{final}\\rangle = a|00\\rangle + b|11\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|01\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now let us consider the third circuit shown, using X gates for Pauli twirling. We could simply multiply the matrices together and verify that they yield a CNOT matrix. Alternatively, we can track the operation on an arbitrary quantum state through the circuit, as we do below. The states at different points in the circuit have been labeled a-d.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang mari kita pertimbangkan litar ketiga yang ditunjukkan, menggunakan get X untuk Pauli twirling. Kita boleh sekadar mendarabkan matriks bersama-sama dan mengesahkan bahawa mereka menghasilkan matriks CNOT. Sebagai alternatif, kita boleh mengesan operasi pada keadaan kuantum sewenang-wenangnya melalui litar, seperti yang kita lakukan di bawah. Keadaan pada titik berbeza dalam litar telah dilabelkan a-d.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A CNOT operation on a two-qubit quantum circuit, surrounded by three X gates. Points are labeled a-d at the beginning of the circuit, after an X gate on the control qubit, after the CNOT gate, and after a final X gate is applied to each of the two qubits, respectively.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/twirl-steps.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A CNOT operation on a two-qubit quantum circuit, surrounded by three X gates. Points are labeled a-d at the beginning of the circuit, after an X gate on the control qubit, after the CNOT gate, and after a final X gate is applied to each of the two qubits, respectively.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/twirl-steps.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_a\\rangle = a|00\\rangle + b|01\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_b\\rangle = a|01\\rangle + b|00\\rangle + c|11\\rangle + d|10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_c\\rangle = a|11\\rangle + b|00\\rangle + c|01\\rangle + d|10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = a|00\\rangle + b|11\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|01\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_a\\rangle = a|00\\rangle + b|01\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_b\\rangle = a|01\\rangle + b|00\\rangle + c|11\\rangle + d|10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_c\\rangle = a|11\\rangle + b|00\\rangle + c|01\\rangle + d|10\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle = a|00\\rangle + b|11\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|01\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is exactly $|\\psi_\\text{final}\\rangle$ that we obtained before with no twirling. Indeed, this twirled gate sequence leaves the logical action of the payload unchanged. However, if different valid twirling sequences are selected randomly from layer to layer, coherent error accumulation can be converted into effectively stochastic (incoherent) error accumulation. To be clear, one does not choose a single twirling pattern and use it throughout the circuit. Instead, different valid twirling sequences are selected for different layers. An example with many entangling layers might look like this.\n"
msgstr "Ini adalah tepat $|\\psi_\\text{final}\\rangle$ yang kita peroleh sebelum ini tanpa twirling. Sesungguhnya, jujukan get yang di-twirl ini meninggalkan tindakan logik muatan tidak berubah. Walau bagaimanapun, jika jujukan twirling yang sah berbeza dipilih secara rawak dari lapisan ke lapisan, pengumpulan ralat koheren boleh ditukar menjadi pengumpulan ralat stokastik (tidak koheren) secara berkesan. Untuk kejelasan, seseorang tidak memilih satu corak twirling dan menggunakannya sepanjang litar. Sebaliknya, jujukan twirling yang sah berbeza dipilih untuk lapisan yang berbeza. Contoh dengan banyak lapisan penjeratan mungkin kelihatan seperti ini.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit with four qubits and three CNOT gates in a ladder arrangement. In twirling, each of these CNOT gates is surrounded by a different set of Pauli gates.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/twirl-mult.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit with four qubits and three CNOT gates in a ladder arrangement. In twirling, each of these CNOT gates is surrounded by a different set of Pauli gates.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/twirl-mult.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Check your understanding {#check-your-understanding-3}"
msgstr "Semak kefahaman anda {#check-your-understanding-3}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify that the Pauli twirling in the fourth panel in the figure above also leaves the logical effect of the CNOT unchanged.\n"
msgstr "Sahkan bahawa Pauli twirling dalam panel keempat dalam rajah di atas juga meninggalkan kesan logik CNOT tidak berubah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We follow the example above and show that the action on any arbitrary two-qubit state is equivalent to a CNOT operation. We will refer to the labeled points in this diagram.\n"
msgstr "Kami mengikut contoh di atas dan menunjukkan bahawa tindakan pada mana-mana keadaan dua-qubit sewenang-wenangnya adalah setara dengan operasi CNOT. Kami akan merujuk kepada titik berlabel dalam gambar rajah ini.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A quantum circuit with two qubits. The initial state is labeled \"a\", then an X gate acts on qubit 0 and a Y gate acts on qubit 1. After that, the state is labeled \"b\". Then a CNOT gate acts with qubit 0 as the control and qubit 1 as the target. After that, CNOT gate the state is labeled \"c\". Finally, a Y gate acts on qubit 0 and a Z gate acts on qubit 1. The final state is labeled \"d\".](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/twirl-check.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A quantum circuit with two qubits. The initial state is labeled \"a\", then an X gate acts on qubit 0 and a Y gate acts on qubit 1. After that, the state is labeled \"b\". Then a CNOT gate acts with qubit 0 as the control and qubit 1 as the target. After that, CNOT gate the state is labeled \"c\". Finally, a Y gate acts on qubit 0 and a Z gate acts on qubit 1. The final state is labeled \"d\".](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/twirl-check.avif)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|\\psi_a\\rangle & = a|00\\rangle + b|01\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_b\\rangle & = ai|11\\rangle + bi|10\\rangle - ci|01\\rangle - di|00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_c\\rangle & = ai|01\\rangle + bi|10\\rangle - ci|11\\rangle - di|00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle & = ai(+1)(-i)|00\\rangle + bi(-1)(i)|11\\rangle - ci(-1)(-i)|10\\rangle - di(+1)(i)|01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle & = a|00\\rangle + b|11\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|01\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"|\\psi_a\\rangle & = a|00\\rangle + b|01\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|11\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_b\\rangle & = ai|11\\rangle + bi|10\\rangle - ci|01\\rangle - di|00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_c\\rangle & = ai|01\\rangle + bi|10\\rangle - ci|11\\rangle - di|00\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle & = ai(+1)(-i)|00\\rangle + bi(-1)(i)|11\\rangle - ci(-1)(-i)|10\\rangle - di(+1)(i)|01\\rangle\\\\\n"
"|\\psi_d\\rangle & = a|00\\rangle + b|11\\rangle + c|10\\rangle + d|01\\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This is equivalent to the action of a CNOT with qubit 0 as the control and qubit 1 as the target.\n"
msgstr "Ini setara dengan tindakan CNOT dengan qubit 0 sebagai kawalan dan qubit 1 sebagai sasaran.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Can you come up with a Pauli twirling sequence for the CNOT gate which is not shown above?\n"
msgstr "Bolehkah anda mencipta jujukan Pauli twirling untuk get CNOT yang tidak ditunjukkan di atas?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Yes, there are many others. One example is $Z_t$ before the CNOT, and a $Z_t$ and $Z_c$ after the CNOT.\n"
msgstr "Ya, terdapat banyak yang lain. Satu contoh ialah $Z_t$ sebelum CNOT, dan $Z_t$ dan $Z_c$ selepas CNOT.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "When to use Pauli twirling {#when-to-use-pauli-twirling}"
msgstr "Bila menggunakan Pauli twirling {#when-to-use-pauli-twirling}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "As presented here, Pauli twirling is applied only to multi-qubit gates. Applying a similar protocol to single-qubit gates would require different logic and is generally not useful in practice. Pauli twirling itself uses several single-qubit gates (the Pauli gates). The additional Pauli gates would likely introduce more error than would be gained by randomizing any coherent error accumulation. Error rates associated with two-qubit gates are much larger than those associated with single-qubit gates. Further, some single-qubit gates are non-Clifford, which cannot be fully twirled. This is why Qiskit includes Pauli twirling options that automatically twirl around two-qubit gates, and not around single-qubit gates.\n"
msgstr "Seperti yang dibentangkan di sini, Pauli twirling hanya digunakan pada get berbilang-qubit. Menggunakan protokol yang serupa pada get satu-qubit memerlukan logik yang berbeza dan amnya tidak berguna dalam praktik. Pauli twirling sendiri menggunakan beberapa get satu-qubit (get Pauli). Get Pauli tambahan berkemungkinan memperkenalkan lebih banyak ralat berbanding yang diperolehi daripada merawakkan mana-mana pengumpulan ralat koheren. Kadar ralat yang dikaitkan dengan get dua-qubit adalah jauh lebih besar berbanding yang dikaitkan dengan get satu-qubit. Selanjutnya, sesetengah get satu-qubit adalah bukan-Clifford, yang tidak boleh di-twirl sepenuhnya. Inilah sebabnya Qiskit merangkumi pilihan Pauli twirling yang secara automatik men-twirl mengelilingi get dua-qubit, dan bukan mengelilingi get satu-qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This was implicit in the figure above: Pauli twirling was implemented around the CX gates, but not around the Hadamard gate.\n"
msgstr "Ini tersirat dalam rajah di atas: Pauli twirling dilaksanakan mengelilingi get CX, tetapi tidak mengelilingi get Hadamard.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Let's see two examples of Pauli twirling in action.\n"
msgstr "Mari kita lihat dua contoh Pauli twirling beraksi.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling to suppress coherent accumulation {#pauli-twirling-to-suppress-coherent-accumulation}"
msgstr "Pauli twirling untuk menyekat pengumpulan koheren {#pauli-twirling-to-suppress-coherent-accumulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To observe how Pauli twirling can turn coherent error accumulation into slower incoherent accumulation, we want a circuit and observable that function as a coherent-error stress test. The sole purpose is to make coherently accumulating two‑qubit errors visible, and then show how Pauli twirling converts that coherent buildup into stochastic decay.\n"
msgstr "Untuk memerhati bagaimana Pauli twirling boleh menukar pengumpulan ralat koheren kepada pengumpulan tidak koheren yang lebih perlahan, kami mahukan litar dan boleh cerap yang berfungsi sebagai ujian tekanan ralat-koheren. Tujuan tunggalnya adalah untuk menjadikan ralat dua-qubit yang terkumpul secara koheren kelihatan, dan kemudian menunjukkan bagaimana Pauli twirling menukar pengumpulan koheren itu kepada kereputan stokastik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "CNOT (or CZ) gates are a common source of coherent errors. The simplest experiment we can do in this case is to initialize a state (say $|+\\rangle$), apply layers of paired CNOT gates (using the fact that two CNOTs yield an identity), and check how errors accumulate as the number of layers increases, both with and without Pauli twirling.\n"
msgstr "Get CNOT (atau CZ) adalah sumber ralat koheren yang biasa. Eksperimen paling mudah yang boleh kami lakukan dalam kes ini adalah untuk memulakan keadaan (katakan $|+\\rangle$), menggunakan lapisan get CNOT berpasangan (menggunakan fakta bahawa dua CNOT menghasilkan identiti), dan menyemak bagaimana ralat terkumpul apabila bilangan lapisan meningkat, kedua-duanya dengan dan tanpa Pauli twirling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The observable of interest is $\\langle X \\rangle$ on a single qubit, which we plot as a function of the number of repetitions of CNOT pairs.\n"
msgstr "Boleh cerap yang menarik minat ialah $\\langle X \\rangle$ pada satu qubit, yang kami plotkan sebagai fungsi bilangan pengulangan pasangan CNOT.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because we have rotated our basis before measurements, a measurement of $|0\\rangle$ corresponds to the state having been in $|+\\rangle$ just before the final Hadamard gate, and similar for $|1\\rangle$ and $|-\\rangle$. Therefore, our expectation value $\\langle X \\rangle$ can be simply calculated from the counts of $|0\\rangle$ minus the counts of $|1\\rangle$.\n"
msgstr "Kerana kami telah memutar asas kami sebelum pengukuran, pengukuran $|0\\rangle$ sepadan dengan keadaan yang berada dalam $|+\\rangle$ sejurus sebelum get Hadamard akhir, dan serupa untuk $|1\\rangle$ dan $|-\\rangle$. Oleh itu, nilai jangkaan kami $\\langle X \\rangle$ boleh dikira dengan mudah daripada kiraan $|0\\rangle$ ditolak kiraan $|1\\rangle$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We select a reasonable number of CNOT layers over which to allow the error to accumulate, build our circuits, then transpile them.\n"
msgstr "Kami memilih bilangan lapisan CNOT yang munasabah untuk membenarkan ralat terkumpul, membina litar kami, kemudian mentranspilnya.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Keep in mind that each layer consists of more than one two-qubit gate. Monitor the transpiled, two-qubit depth by using the function below.\n"
msgstr "Ingat bahawa setiap lapisan terdiri daripada lebih daripada satu get dua-qubit. Pantau kedalaman dua-qubit yang ditranspil dengan menggunakan fungsi di bawah.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we run the jobs.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami menjalankan job.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we visualize these results.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, kami memvisualisasikan hasil ini.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/abf5ce16-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/abf5ce16-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can clearly see that the twirled circuit yields an expectation value closer to the ideal $\\langle X \\rangle = 1$. This example served its purpose, but let's move onto something more useful: twirling in the production of highly entangled states.\n"
msgstr "Kami boleh melihat dengan jelas bahawa litar yang di-twirl menghasilkan nilai jangkaan yang lebih hampir dengan ideal $\\langle X \\rangle = 1$. Contoh ini memenuhi tujuannya, tetapi mari kita beralih kepada sesuatu yang lebih berguna: twirling dalam penghasilan keadaan yang sangat terjerat.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling in GHZ state preparation {#pauli-twirling-in-ghz-state-preparation}"
msgstr "Pauli twirling dalam penyediaan keadaan GHZ {#pauli-twirling-in-ghz-state-preparation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The previous example showed a compelling case for Pauli twirling in destroying the coherent accumulation of errors associated with CNOT gates. GHZ state production uses many CNOT gates to produce highly entangled states useful for many quantum computing applications. Let's explore how Pauli twirling helps in this context, with GHZ states of increasing size.\n"
msgstr "Contoh sebelumnya menunjukkan kes yang meyakinkan untuk Pauli twirling dalam memusnahkan pengumpulan koheren ralat yang dikaitkan dengan get CNOT. Penghasilan keadaan GHZ menggunakan banyak get CNOT untuk menghasilkan keadaan yang sangat terjerat yang berguna untuk banyak aplikasi pengkomputeran kuantum. Mari kita terokai bagaimana Pauli twirling membantu dalam konteks ini, dengan keadaan GHZ yang saiznya semakin meningkat.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/25f23671-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/25f23671-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we build our circuits and transpile them. In this case, we don't have any artificially repeated gates that reduce to the identity. So we can allow the pass manager to do a bit more optimizing for us. We'll set it to level three.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami membina litar kami dan mentranspilnya. Dalam kes ini, kami tidak mempunyai sebarang get berulang secara buatan yang berkurangan kepada identiti. Jadi kami boleh membenarkan pass manager melakukan sedikit lebih pengoptimuman untuk kami. Kami akan menetapkannya kepada tahap tiga.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We can see that the optimizer mapped our abstract circuit to qubits 123, 124, 136, 142, and 143.\n"
msgstr "Kami boleh melihat bahawa pengoptimum memetakan litar abstrak kami kepada qubit 123, 124, 136, 142, dan 143.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/2100ead4-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/2100ead4-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To understand why, let's look at a map of the layout of our backend (in this image, `ibm_fez`, but you can do equivalent analyses on any backend).\n"
msgstr "Untuk memahami sebabnya, mari kita lihat peta susun atur backend kami (dalam imej ini, `ibm_fez`, tetapi anda boleh melakukan analisis setara pada mana-mana backend).\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![A diagram of the layout of qubits on a quantum computer called ibm_fez. It shows how qubits are chosen to minimize swapping of information.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/ghz-transpile.avif)\n"
msgstr "![A diagram of the layout of qubits on a quantum computer called ibm_fez. It shows how qubits are chosen to minimize swapping of information.](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/ghz-transpile.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We see that the qubits were selected in a chain to minimize swap gates and thus circuit depth. Further, each CZ gate implemented in the circuit is between adjacent qubits. Finally, all five qubits have relatively low error rates, including readout-assignment error rates. You can check these error rates on any backend on the [Compute resources](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers) page. Finding such a layout is not difficult for a simple linear chain, but as problems become more complex, the optimization of the circuit layout becomes more difficult and more valuable.\n"
msgstr "Kita lihat bahawa qubit dipilih dalam rantai untuk meminimumkan get swap dan dengan itu kedalaman litar. Selanjutnya, setiap get CZ yang dilaksanakan dalam litar adalah antara qubit bersebelahan. Akhir sekali, kesemua lima qubit mempunyai kadar ralat yang agak rendah, termasuk kadar ralat penetapan-bacaan. Anda boleh menyemak kadar ralat ini pada mana-mana backend pada halaman [Sumber pengkomputeran](https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/computers). Mencari susun atur sedemikian tidak sukar untuk rantai linear yang mudah, tetapi apabila masalah menjadi lebih kompleks, pengoptimuman susun atur litar menjadi lebih sukar dan lebih bernilai.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we configure our Sampler primitive. We turn off other suppression/mitigation tools to focus on Pauli twirling.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami mengkonfigurasi primitif Sampler kami. Kami mematikan alat penyekatan/mitigasi lain untuk memfokus pada Pauli twirling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, we run our jobs. You can optionally print the job ID numbers for later retrieval.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya, kami menjalankan job kami. Anda boleh secara pilihan mencetak nombor ID job untuk pengambilan semula kemudian.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We extract the counts of each computational basis state measured for all the circuits, both with and without twirling.\n"
msgstr "Kami mengekstrak kiraan setiap keadaan asas pengkomputeran yang diukur untuk semua litar, kedua-duanya dengan dan tanpa twirling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We know the ideal distribution of a GHZ state is that in which half the shots return $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$ and the other half return $|1\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$. Build this for comparison.\n"
msgstr "Kami tahu taburan ideal keadaan GHZ ialah separuh daripada shot mengembalikan $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$ dan separuh lagi mengembalikan $|1\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$. Bina ini untuk perbandingan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We now use the Hellinger fidelity as a measure of the quality of our final state.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kami menggunakan ketepatan Hellinger sebagai ukuran kualiti keadaan akhir kami.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally we plot our results.\n"
msgstr "Akhirnya kami plotkan hasil kami.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/879b4eb0-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/879b4eb0-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The results using Pauli twirling are no better (and even slightly worse) than without twirling. What happened?\n"
msgstr "Hasil menggunakan Pauli twirling tidak lebih baik (dan malah sedikit lebih teruk) berbanding tanpa twirling. Apa yang berlaku?\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Two things happened. First, Pauli twirling does not reduce the total amount of noise &mdash; rather, it reshapes coherent, systematic errors into stochastic Pauli‑type errors, so that error growth becomes predictable and modelable. There was never any promise of error reduction, except in special cases.\n"
msgstr "Dua perkara berlaku. Pertama, Pauli twirling tidak mengurangkan jumlah hingar keseluruhan &mdash; sebaliknya, ia membentuk semula ralat koheren dan sistematik kepada ralat jenis Pauli stokastik, supaya pertumbuhan ralat menjadi boleh diramal dan boleh dimodelkan. Tidak pernah ada janji pengurangan ralat, kecuali dalam kes khas.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Secondly, in GHZ circuits, some coherent errors can partially cancel or act like benign phase shifts because of the symmetry of the GHZ construction; twirling removes this accidental protection and replaces it with uncorrelated stochastic Pauli noise, so GHZ fidelity becomes slightly worse under twirling.\n"
msgstr "Kedua, dalam litar GHZ, sesetengah ralat koheren boleh sebahagiannya saling batal atau bertindak seperti anjakan fasa yang tidak berbahaya disebabkan simetri pembinaan GHZ; twirling menghapuskan perlindungan kebetulan ini dan menggantikannya dengan hingar Pauli stokastik yang tidak berkorelasi, jadi ketepatan GHZ menjadi sedikit lebih teruk di bawah twirling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This second claim requires some explanation. The claim is not that GHZ circuits are protected from __all__ kinds of coherent error accumulation, only some kinds &mdash; and that in those cases the protection is destroyed by twirling. Specifically, let's consider coherent over-rotation associated with the CX gates. Let us call the real CX gate with over-rotation $\\tilde{CX}$:\n"
msgstr "Dakwaan kedua ini memerlukan sedikit penjelasan. Dakwaannya bukanlah bahawa litar GHZ dilindungi daripada __semua__ jenis pengumpulan ralat koheren, hanya sesetengah jenis &mdash; dan dalam kes tersebut perlindungan itu dimusnahkan oleh twirling. Secara khusus, mari kita pertimbangkan lebih-putaran koheren yang dikaitkan dengan get CX. Mari kita namakan get CX sebenar dengan lebih-putaran $\\tilde{CX}$:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{CX}\\equiv e^{-i\\epsilon K} \\cdot CX\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{CX}\\equiv e^{-i\\epsilon K} \\cdot CX\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "where $K$ is any product of Pauli operators, like $X$, $Z$, $Z \\otimes X$, $Z^{\\otimes N}$, etc. For general states, any of these over-rotations could affect measurement statistics (and thus measures of state fidelity). A subset of these, however, leaves many standard GHZ observables unchanged, including operators such as $Z_i Z_j$ and $Z^{\\otimes N}$. In the context of preparing a GHZ state, the relevant over-rotation errors of this type would be:\n"
msgstr "dengan $K$ ialah sebarang hasil darab operator Pauli, seperti $X$, $Z$, $Z \\otimes X$, $Z^{\\otimes N}$, dan sebagainya. Untuk keadaan umum, mana-mana putaran-lebih ini boleh menjejaskan statistik pengukuran (dan seterusnya ukuran kesetiaan keadaan). Walau bagaimanapun, sebahagian daripadanya tidak menjejaskan banyak boleh amat GHZ piawai, termasuk operator seperti $Z_i Z_j$ dan $Z^{\\otimes N}$. Dalam konteks penyediaan keadaan GHZ, ralat putaran-lebih jenis ini yang relevan adalah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{CX}\\equiv e^{-i\\epsilon Z_c Z_t} \\cdot CX\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\tilde{CX}\\equiv e^{-i\\epsilon Z_c Z_t} \\cdot CX\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The preparation of the entire $N$-qubit GHZ state would look like:\n"
msgstr "Penyediaan keseluruhan keadaan GHZ $N$-qubit akan kelihatan seperti:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_\\text{GHZ}\\rangle=\\prod_{j=0}^{N-2}{e^{-i\\epsilon Z_j Z_{j+1}} \\cdot CX_{j,j+1}}H^{\\otimes N}|0^{\\otimes N}\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\psi_\\text{GHZ}\\rangle=\\prod_{j=0}^{N-2}{e^{-i\\epsilon Z_j Z_{j+1}} \\cdot CX_{j,j+1}}H^{\\otimes N}|0^{\\otimes N}\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "After preparing the GHZ state, the state is ideally:\n"
msgstr "Selepas menyediakan keadaan GHZ, keadaan tersebut secara ideal adalah:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"|\\text{GHZ}^{\\otimes N}\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\dots 0\\rangle + |1\\dots 1\\rangle\\right).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"|\\text{GHZ}^{\\otimes N}\\rangle=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}}\\left(|0\\dots 0\\rangle + |1\\dots 1\\rangle\\right).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This state is a simultaneous eigenstate of a large set of Pauli operators, including the following:\n"
msgstr "Keadaan ini ialah eigenkeadaan serentak bagi satu set besar operator Pauli, termasuk yang berikut:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i Z_j \\quad \\text{for all } i \\neq j,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"Z_i Z_j \\quad \\text{for all } i \\neq j,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"with eigenvalue $+1$. As a result, an operator of the form $e^{-i\\epsilon Z_i Z_j}$ acts on the GHZ state as multiplication by the phase factor $e^{-i\\epsilon}$, which does not affect standard GHZ observables such as parity, collective $X^{\\otimes N}$, or computational‑basis populations.\n"
"Thus, although the over‑rotation errors $e^{-i\\epsilon Z_j Z_{j+1}}$ are coherent and systematic, they are effectively invisible to the measurements used to assess GHZ fidelity. In this sense, the GHZ circuit enjoys an accidental coherence protection: certain coherent CX errors commute with the structure of the state being prepared and therefore do not degrade measured performance.\n"
msgstr ""
"dengan eigennilai $+1$. Hasilnya, operator dalam bentuk $e^{-i\\epsilon Z_i Z_j}$ bertindak ke atas keadaan GHZ sebagai pendaraban dengan faktor fasa $e^{-i\\epsilon}$, yang tidak menjejaskan boleh amat GHZ piawai seperti pariti, $X^{\\otimes N}$ kolektif, atau populasi asas-pengkomputeran.\n"
"Oleh itu, walaupun ralat putaran-lebih $e^{-i\\epsilon Z_j Z_{j+1}}$ adalah koheren dan sistematik, ia secara efektifnya tidak kelihatan kepada pengukuran yang digunakan untuk menilai kesetiaan GHZ. Dalam erti kata ini, litar GHZ menikmati perlindungan koherens secara kebetulan: sesetengah ralat CX koheren berkomut dengan struktur keadaan yang sedang disediakan dan oleh itu tidak menjejaskan prestasi yang diukur.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling fundamentally changes this situation. Twirling does not preserve the coherent over‑rotation error as a deterministic $Z_jZ_{j+1}$ process. Instead, it converts the coherent error channel into an effective stochastic Pauli channel. As a result, the error channel now includes terms such as $X$, $Y$, $X \\otimes Z$, and $Y \\otimes X$, which do not commute with the GHZ stabilizers.\n"
msgstr "Twirling Pauli secara asasnya mengubah situasi ini. Twirling tidak mengekalkan ralat putaran-lebih koheren sebagai proses $Z_jZ_{j+1}$ yang deterministik. Sebaliknya, ia menukar saluran ralat koheren kepada saluran Pauli stokastik yang efektif. Hasilnya, saluran ralat kini merangkumi terma seperti $X$, $Y$, $X \\otimes Z$, dan $Y \\otimes X$, yang tidak berkomut dengan penstabil GHZ.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "When these stochastic Pauli errors occur, they create real bit‑flip and phase‑flip faults on individual qubits or pairs of qubits. These errors take the state out of the GHZ stabilizer subspace, reduce interference between $|0\\dots 0\\rangle$ and $|1\\dots 1\\rangle$, and directly lower GHZ fidelity and multi‑qubit parity signals. In other words, Pauli twirling removes the coherent structure of the error but also removes the symmetry‑based cancellation that previously made those errors benign. The result is a slightly worse GHZ state &mdash; not because twirling adds noise, but because it converts a mostly harmless coherent error into genuinely damaging stochastic errors.\n"
msgstr "Apabila ralat Pauli stokastik ini berlaku, ia mencipta kegagalan songsang-bit dan songsang-fasa yang sebenar pada qubit individu atau pasangan qubit. Ralat ini mengeluarkan keadaan tersebut daripada subruang penstabil GHZ, mengurangkan interferens antara $|0\\dots 0\\rangle$ dan $|1\\dots 1\\rangle$, dan secara langsung menurunkan kesetiaan GHZ serta isyarat pariti multi-qubit. Dalam erti kata lain, twirling Pauli menghapuskan struktur koheren ralat tetapi turut menghapuskan pembatalan berasaskan simetri yang sebelum ini menjadikan ralat itu tidak berbahaya. Hasilnya ialah keadaan GHZ yang sedikit lebih teruk &mdash; bukan kerana twirling menambah hingar, tetapi kerana ia menukar ralat koheren yang kebanyakannya tidak berbahaya kepada ralat stokastik yang benar-benar merosakkan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This example highlights an important lesson: Pauli twirling is not a universal improvement strategy. It is most beneficial when coherent errors accumulate across a circuit in a manner destructive to the required fidelity. In highly symmetric circuits like GHZ state preparation, some coherent errors are naturally aligned with the state’s stabilizers, and deliberately randomizing them can eliminate this accidental protection.\n"
msgstr "Contoh ini menyerlahkan satu pengajaran penting: twirling Pauli bukan strategi penambahbaikan universal. Ia paling bermanfaat apabila ralat koheren terkumpul sepanjang litar dengan cara yang merosakkan kesetiaan yang diperlukan. Dalam litar yang amat simetri seperti penyediaan keadaan GHZ, sesetengah ralat koheren secara semula jadi selari dengan penstabil keadaan tersebut, dan merawak-acakkan ralat itu secara sengaja boleh menghapuskan perlindungan kebetulan ini.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Combine methods {#combine-methods}"
msgstr "Gabungkan kaedah {#combine-methods}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One can in principle combine Pauli twirling with dynamical decoupling. We have not used DD in this case for two reasons: firstly there should not be any extremely long idle periods in this circuit. Secondly, GHZ states do not store most of their information in single-qubit phase coherence, particularly if we are observing the fidelity only in terms of bitstring counts, and not in terms of the phase between the desired bitstrings $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$ and $|1\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$.\n"
msgstr "Pada dasarnya, seseorang boleh menggabungkan twirling Pauli dengan penyahgandingan dinamik. Kami tidak menggunakan DD dalam kes ini atas dua sebab: pertama, tidak sepatutnya terdapat tempoh diam yang amat panjang dalam litar ini. Kedua, keadaan GHZ tidak menyimpan kebanyakan maklumatnya dalam koheren fasa satu-qubit, terutamanya jika kita hanya memerhatikan kesetiaan dari segi kiraan rentetan-bit, dan bukan dari segi fasa antara rentetan-bit yang dikehendaki $|0\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$ dan $|1\\rangle^{\\otimes N}$.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If we were to extend the GHZ preparation to 100+ qubits, then the delays in measuring the first/early qubits might indeed be long enough that DD could be useful. This is especially true when we take into account the transpiled depth of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Jika kita hendak memanjangkan penyediaan GHZ kepada 100+ qubit, maka kelewatan dalam mengukur qubit pertama/awal mungkin memang cukup panjang sehingga DD boleh berguna. Ini terutamanya benar apabila kita mengambil kira kedalaman litar yang telah ditranspilasi.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-28
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling in RTZ echo structure {#pauli-twirling-in-rtz-echo-structure}"
msgstr "Pauli twirling dalam struktur gema RTZ {#pauli-twirling-in-rtz-echo-structure}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Our final example of Pauli twirling in the context of reducing coherent error accumulation uses a circuit with layers of X-CZ-X-CZ combinations. This is a well-known gate sequence that is often used to cancel coherent ZZ error terms in two-qubit gates, even without twirling. But with twirling, we can reduce or randomize other forms of coherent error accumulation.\n"
msgstr "Contoh terakhir kami bagi twirling Pauli dalam konteks mengurangkan pengumpulan ralat koheren menggunakan litar dengan lapisan gabungan X-CZ-X-CZ. Ini ialah jujukan get yang terkenal yang sering digunakan untuk membatalkan terma ralat ZZ koheren dalam get dua-qubit, walaupun tanpa twirling. Tetapi dengan twirling, kita boleh mengurangkan atau merawak-acakkan bentuk lain pengumpulan ralat koheren.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We'll start by defining a function to build the RTZ-like circuits with a varying number of layers.\n"
msgstr "Kita akan mulakan dengan mentakrifkan fungsi untuk membina litar seakan-RTZ dengan bilangan lapisan yang berbeza-beza.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we build circuits with increasing layers, up to some reasonable total transpiled two-qubit depth.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita membina litar dengan lapisan yang semakin bertambah, sehingga ke kedalaman dua-qubit yang telah ditranspilasi yang munasabah.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/7027c76d-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/7027c76d-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "At the high end, some of these are quite deep. Let's use the AerSimulator with no noise model to obtain the ideal states at the end of each of these circuits. We can then can benchmark our results from real quantum computers using the Hellinger fidelity.\n"
msgstr "Pada hujung yang tinggi, sesetengah daripadanya agak dalam. Mari kita gunakan AerSimulator tanpa model hingar untuk mendapatkan keadaan ideal pada penghujung setiap litar ini. Kita kemudiannya boleh menanda aras keputusan kita daripada komputer kuantum sebenar menggunakan kesetiaan Hellinger.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we define a SamplerV2 with twirling, and one without twirling.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita mentakrifkan SamplerV2 dengan twirling, dan satu lagi tanpa twirling.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we run our jobs.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita menjalankan job kita.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "We get the counts from each of the runs on a real quantum computer.\n"
msgstr "Kita mendapatkan kiraan daripada setiap larian pada komputer kuantum sebenar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we find the Hellinger fidelity by comparing each of these runs to the noise-free AerSimulator results.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita mencari kesetiaan Hellinger dengan membandingkan setiap larian ini dengan keputusan AerSimulator bebas-hingar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Now we visualize our results.\n"
msgstr "Sekarang kita menggambarkan keputusan kita.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/548a0f1c-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/learning/images/courses/tools-for-quantum-advantage/error-suppression/extracted-outputs/548a0f1c-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Throughout this lesson, we have examined cases in which Pauli twirling is used to limit coherent error accumulation, a context in which it might be described as *error suppression*. However, Pauli twirling is often more useful as a tool for reshaping error behavior, converting coherent errors into a form that is more predictable and easier to model. The usefulness of this will become more apparent in the context of error-mitigation techniques such as zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE), which rely on reasonably predictable noise scaling. This is discussed in the next lesson.\n"
msgstr "Sepanjang pelajaran ini, kita telah meneliti kes di mana twirling Pauli digunakan untuk mengehadkan pengumpulan ralat koheren, konteks di mana ia mungkin diterangkan sebagai *penindasan ralat*. Walau bagaimanapun, twirling Pauli sering lebih berguna sebagai alat untuk membentuk semula tingkah laku ralat, menukar ralat koheren kepada bentuk yang lebih boleh diramal dan lebih mudah dimodelkan. Kegunaan ini akan menjadi lebih jelas dalam konteks teknik mitigasi ralat seperti ekstrapolasi hingar-sifar (ZNE), yang bergantung pada penskalaan hingar yang agak boleh diramal. Ini dibincangkan dalam pelajaran seterusnya.\n"
